WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:05.200
Hi, welcome back to the last session--
[Yay!!!]--

00:00:06.440 --> 00:00:10.800
of the at-home Wheel of Life retreat.

00:00:13.080 --> 00:00:19.120
We've been through
a pretty major amount of the lam rim (LAM RIM),

00:00:22.600 --> 00:00:25.840
in twenty-four different sessions.

00:00:27.960 --> 00:00:37.160
And probably as you remember, we've looked at a lot of pictures or images as we went through.

00:00:41.480 --> 00:00:49.720
And in English we have an expression:
One picture is worth a thousand words.

00:00:51.040 --> 00:00:55.920
So what I'd like to do in this last class,

00:00:57.960 --> 00:01:05.080
out of all the many pictures
that we used in these twenty-four sessions so far--

00:01:11.040 --> 00:01:19.080
I chose twelve, and these are the most important pictures from this whole course.

00:01:22.040 --> 00:01:26.080
You can sort of do a self-examination here at the end.

00:01:30.960 --> 00:01:36.520
I think if you remember
what these twelve pictures represent,

00:01:40.800 --> 00:01:45.480
then you are remembering
all the important points of this whole course.

00:01:49.600 --> 00:01:54.480
I have a special nickname I gave to these pictures.

00:01:56.240 --> 00:02:00.760
I call them idim, which is I-D-I-M.

00:02:02.480 --> 00:02:07.000
That's a short word for "idea image."

00:02:09.840 --> 00:02:14.320
They also say Chinese language characters,

00:02:17.800 --> 00:02:26.360
some people say why Chinese people are so smart, except all of them. Not all of them, I mean.

00:02:29.160 --> 00:02:37.600
Just kidding.
But they say that Chinese people think in pictures, in a way.

00:02:40.160 --> 00:02:46.800
And I think it's kind of true.
So I want you to think in pictures.

00:02:48.240 --> 00:02:53.120
I'm not going to make it too many.
Just twelve.

00:02:54.520 --> 00:03:00.520
I've been teaching this lam rim for ten years.

00:03:01.760 --> 00:03:07.560
I think we have another six years to go for this book.

00:03:09.560 --> 00:03:18.600
Then dessert. How many? We said thirteen years, Tim? Yeah, thirteen years dessert, if you want.

00:03:20.760 --> 00:03:26.720
shamatha and vipashyana dessert for thirteen more years.

00:03:30.120 --> 00:03:36.880
And what I've done is I've collected together images from all of those ten years.

00:03:41.360 --> 00:03:45.640
And we'll be doing some
separate videos about those images.

00:03:47.920 --> 00:03:55.200
If you can remember all of those images
from the last ten years,

00:03:59.080 --> 00:04:04.040
then even if you couldn't come to every lam rim retreat--we had thirty-four already--

00:04:12.200 --> 00:04:16.160
pretty much you would understand the content.

00:04:19.120 --> 00:04:22.720
Okay, let's get going through these twelve idims.

00:04:24.480 --> 00:04:31.760
The first picture you see here,
it's a guy doing something to a bomb.

00:04:33.480 --> 00:04:39.200
We would say he's turning on the bomb.

00:04:40.320 --> 00:04:49.080
He's setting the timer.
Then he will run away and that bomb will explode
after five minutes or something.

00:04:51.960 --> 00:04:57.800
And one of the most important parts
of this Wheel of Life course,

00:05:02.280 --> 00:05:10.120
we talked about how a seed is "triggered" or "armed"

00:05:12.760 --> 00:05:21.080
at the last minute of your life,
and that's a crucial moment in our life.

00:05:22.600 --> 00:05:25.920
The last minute of awareness of this world.

00:05:30.080 --> 00:05:41.960
In a way, we are selecting and we are waking up the seed which is going to send us into our new life--or create our new life.

00:05:52.920 --> 00:06:02.680
The name of this first idim is
"Activation, Priorities, Earlier, Habit, Closer, Serious."

00:06:10.160 --> 00:06:15.080
There's just four principles I want you to remember.

00:06:17.160 --> 00:06:33.600
Generally speaking, on your deathbed, the seed that will open will be the earliest one you planted.

00:06:36.600 --> 00:06:42.520
First-in, first-out.
So of course we want it to be a good seed.

00:06:43.040 --> 00:06:48.800
I was trying to remember the earliest good seed
I ever planted in this life.

00:06:52.040 --> 00:06:58.600
And I kind of realized that little kids don't really care about planting good seeds.

00:07:02.400 --> 00:07:06.080
But I did enjoy making my mom happy.

00:07:11.160 --> 00:07:20.000
Generally speaking as we die the...
hopefully the earlier good seeds we planted should open.

00:07:26.080 --> 00:07:29.280
But there's an exception to that rule.

00:07:30.240 --> 00:07:33.040
If later in your life,

00:07:35.440 --> 00:07:41.280
you had a good habit and you did something
over, and over, and over again,

00:07:43.720 --> 00:07:51.920
then that seed will move up in front of the line to that other seed and it will open first.

00:07:56.160 --> 00:08:01.880
Unless--and here we went to the Abhidharma literature,

00:08:04.000 --> 00:08:14.080
it's possible for a very emotional moment
at the end of your life to come first in line.

00:08:20.040 --> 00:08:27.880
And that's why we try to encourage our loved ones to have good thoughts as they die.

00:08:34.040 --> 00:08:38.400
But if they did some very huge good deed in their life,

00:08:43.160 --> 00:08:51.800
like they saw emptiness directly, or they had an experience of love for all beings in the universe,

00:08:54.720 --> 00:08:58.400
then that seed will take over when we die.

00:09:01.520 --> 00:09:06.760
So I what I want you to remember
when you see this picture, this idim,

00:09:10.760 --> 00:09:14.640
I want you to think about
the good things you did in your life,

00:09:16.160 --> 00:09:22.000
and especially try to remember
the biggest, biggest good things you did.

00:09:24.920 --> 00:09:29.800
The second of the twelve idims for this course,

00:09:32.120 --> 00:09:36.760
it's a picture of a woman making a phone call,

00:09:39.000 --> 00:09:43.000
and there's a piece of glass next to her.

00:09:46.360 --> 00:09:54.840
The name of the idim is
"Peacefully Reminding Them of Good--During and After."

00:10:00.720 --> 00:10:07.600
It means, while your loved one is in the hospital dying--

00:10:12.640 --> 00:10:17.960
for my dad, he was very ill for about six weeks,

00:10:19.880 --> 00:10:26.960
so I took the chance to remind him
of all the good things he did in his life.

00:10:29.240 --> 00:10:34.120
"Dad, what was the earliest good thing
you remember that you did?

00:10:36.920 --> 00:10:44.680
Or did you go through a part of your life where you did a certain good thing over and over for a couple years?

00:10:49.840 --> 00:10:56.240
Or is there some special thing you could think about right now that would be a really good karma?

00:11:00.240 --> 00:11:04.000
And Dad, what was the best thing you ever did?"

00:11:05.520 --> 00:11:21.480
Then dad passed. And the second half of this idim is that you can talk to dead people. They are in the bardo (BAR DO).

00:11:25.920 --> 00:11:30.360
We found out they have special powers at that time--

00:11:33.680 --> 00:11:41.320
they can hear you and they can even see you, like looking through a glass, but they cannot touch you or talk to you.

00:11:45.840 --> 00:11:52.800
So keep talking to them. You can help them.
It's called jang chok (BYANG CHOG).

00:11:53.400 --> 00:11:58.720
Just keep talking to them
about all the good things they did.

00:11:59.960 --> 00:12:09.440
You can do a very powerful good deed
to help your loved ones to take a good rebirth.

00:12:15.520 --> 00:12:22.640
The next item I'd like to use
is a picture of the Wheel of Life.

00:12:24.720 --> 00:12:28.080
I call it a "Blueprint for Pain."

00:12:29.960 --> 00:12:37.720
It includes all the secrets about
why do we have trouble in this life,
why do we have to die.

00:12:44.120 --> 00:12:49.560
We focused on the twelve links around the outside of the circle,

00:12:53.680 --> 00:13:01.040
and there's really three of the twelve links
that I want you to particularly remember.

00:13:04.760 --> 00:13:08.600
Remember, link number one is the big trouble.

00:13:09.720 --> 00:13:12.320
What is it in the kitchen?

00:13:13.040 --> 00:13:21.760
Yeah, "He's yelling at me. I didn't do anything!"
That's a misunderstanding. That plants a bad seed.

00:13:22.800 --> 00:13:26.000
Then if you don't study more,

00:13:27.680 --> 00:13:30.320
if you don't practice more,

00:13:31.640 --> 00:13:37.960
that seed will get water and fertilizer
at link number eight and link number nine.

00:13:41.120 --> 00:13:43.800
And it will take you to a bad place.

00:13:45.000 --> 00:13:51.720
So first of all, never never think
"I didn't do anything."

00:13:52.920 --> 00:14:01.680
Everything in your life is coming from what you did.
And be careful to keep studying emptiness.

00:14:04.560 --> 00:14:10.840
Keep studying vipashyana,
keep studying shamatha meditation.

00:14:15.360 --> 00:14:18.040
Keep doing good things for other people.

00:14:19.680 --> 00:14:27.120
And those three have a kind of power to block your bad seeds and help your good seeds open.

00:14:32.000 --> 00:14:42.000
Okay idim number four.
We did not cover this one--the picture--during the course.

00:14:44.120 --> 00:14:52.880
But I got this picture separately.
It shows a seed opening into a sprout.

00:14:58.120 --> 00:15:05.320
And I chose it because I want you to remember the Shalistambha sutra [Śālistamba sūtra].

00:15:09.880 --> 00:15:18.880
The "Sprout of Rice Sutra."
This is the famous source of the teaching on the links.

00:15:23.280 --> 00:15:27.800
And when you see this idim, this picture,

00:15:28.800 --> 00:15:37.040
please, I want you to remember the opening lines
of that sutra for the idea of dependence.

00:15:41.080 --> 00:15:48.920
Buddha said, "If this thing is here,
then that thing is going to happen."

00:15:49.320 --> 00:15:52.480
Cause and effect.
因果
Yīnguǒ

00:15:53.120 --> 00:15:59.600
That's all.
If this is here, that's going to happen.

00:16:01.840 --> 00:16:07.440
If you ever think
to blame another person for your problems,

00:16:14.120 --> 00:16:18.000
then you are making karma,
which will cause you to suffer.

00:16:19.960 --> 00:16:23.120
Okay, so this seed and this sprout,

00:16:24.000 --> 00:16:35.080
it's a reminder of the sutra where the Buddha first said, "everything is your fault."

00:16:36.120 --> 00:16:42.160
Don't blame other people for your problems.
Fix your problems.

00:16:43.120 --> 00:16:45.200
Okay, idim number five.

00:16:46.120 --> 00:16:49.680
I chose a picture of my dog.

00:16:51.160 --> 00:16:55.000
I took that picture two or three days ago.

00:16:56.400 --> 00:16:59.560
And something happened to him.

00:17:00.160 --> 00:17:08.040
He got blind and deaf and also his smell doesn't work--within one week.

00:17:11.640 --> 00:17:18.440
He is always walking around the house
and he hits his head.

00:17:19.000 --> 00:17:22.280
You can see he has a flat head.
So that's lucky.

00:17:24.720 --> 00:17:30.080
We put pillows everywhere,

00:17:31.000 --> 00:17:34.720
but still he finds some place to hit his head.

00:17:37.240 --> 00:17:40.920
What this idim represents to me,

00:17:42.840 --> 00:17:47.440
is if you are blind,
you're going to hit your head.

00:17:47.800 --> 00:17:51.680
Which means, "I didn't do anything!"

00:17:52.120 --> 00:17:56.520
Then you're going to hit your head.
You're going to get trouble.

00:17:57.000 --> 00:18:03.640
All of us have problems,
all of us meet people we don't like.

00:18:04.800 --> 00:18:09.560
All of us have bad experiences with people we don't like,

00:18:13.520 --> 00:18:17.480
but if you understand this course,

00:18:19.160 --> 00:18:23.600
you will think, "I must have planted this."

00:18:25.640 --> 00:18:30.280
And what's your action plan after you understand "I planted this"?

00:18:32.120 --> 00:18:35.320
Extremely simple.

00:18:36.440 --> 00:18:44.200
What the other person is doing that you don't like,
stop doing it yourself and they will go away.

00:18:52.960 --> 00:18:55.760
So you don't need a lot of philosophy.

00:18:56.840 --> 00:18:59.920
Any bad things that happen to you,

00:19:01.400 --> 00:19:04.000
especially problems with other people,

00:19:06.280 --> 00:19:11.080
choose what it is that you don't like the most about this.

00:19:13.280 --> 00:19:15.680
And your action plan:

00:19:16.160 --> 00:19:20.120
stop doing that thing yourself.

00:19:21.280 --> 00:19:27.760
Don't worry about the other person.
If you stop doing that thing yourself,

00:19:28.520 --> 00:19:30.480
they will move away.

00:19:30.560 --> 00:19:32.000
They will die.

00:19:32.120 --> 00:19:34.000
They will become your friend.

00:19:34.000 --> 00:19:36.120
Something will happen.

00:19:36.600 --> 00:19:38.600
Okay, next idim.

00:19:39.960 --> 00:19:44.480
I have Shakespeare here,

00:19:45.200 --> 00:19:50.040
and I have a picture of a bunch of cogs or gears.

00:19:52.240 --> 00:20:01.000
And the name of the idim is "It's Not as Easy as Shakespeare's Stages."

00:20:04.520 --> 00:20:14.120
What I mean is, we're referring to a famous quotation from Shakespeare about the stages of a person's life.

00:20:21.520 --> 00:20:26.120
And really, it's very, very powerful poetry.

00:20:28.080 --> 00:20:35.040
I think it's some of the only
Buddhist writing in English ever.

00:20:41.320 --> 00:20:47.000
And he says look, everyone goes through the same stages.

00:20:48.160 --> 00:20:51.640
First there's a little kid pooping everywhere.

00:20:51.960 --> 00:20:58.080
Then they're romantic,
they fall in love with all the girls or boys.

00:20:59.320 --> 00:21:03.520
Then they become a patriot
and they want to fight the other countries.

00:21:05.760 --> 00:21:11.520
Then they get rich and fat if they survive the war.

00:21:13.280 --> 00:21:20.120
Then they become again like a kid--
stupid, can't remember anything,

00:21:22.040 --> 00:21:24.080
body is very weak,

00:21:24.640 --> 00:21:26.520
and then they die.

00:21:26.800 --> 00:21:31.440
And Shakespeare says everybody's story is this.

00:21:32.720 --> 00:21:36.600
So that part is good, I like Shakespeare for that.

00:21:37.920 --> 00:21:43.200
But don't think our Wheel of Life is like that Shakespeare.

00:21:45.600 --> 00:21:52.560
Why? We are not talking about twelve stages of human life.

00:21:54.440 --> 00:21:59.120
We're talking about stage one trigger another wheel, stage two trigger another wheel, stage three trigger another wheel

00:21:59.200 --> 00:22:05.600
another wheel trigger, another wheel trigger...
trigger, trigger, trigger.... all kinds of wheels going.

00:22:12.120 --> 00:22:17.080
Everything you do is going to trigger a hundred other things.

00:22:18.640 --> 00:22:22.360
It's not that you go through one wheel in your life.

00:22:24.800 --> 00:22:29.320
In fact, we said it's impossible
to finish a wheel in one life.

00:22:32.240 --> 00:22:41.000
At least two lives. Maximum three lives, but it means maximum of a thousand different wheels.

00:22:45.040 --> 00:22:48.080
Okay the next idim,

00:22:48.920 --> 00:22:51.480
which is number seven here,

00:22:52.120 --> 00:23:00.680
a guy is turning on a landmine
and he hopes his enemy will step on it one week later.

00:23:06.120 --> 00:23:11.160
And the principal I want you
to remember from this picture--

00:23:13.680 --> 00:23:19.080
it says "Army Landmine--Radiation not Sunlight."

00:23:25.560 --> 00:23:32.960
And what does it mean? It's very simple.
When you do coffee meditation at night,

00:23:35.080 --> 00:23:39.320
thinking about the good seed
that you planted when you helped somebody,

00:23:42.120 --> 00:23:48.880
that happy feeling is like sunlight,
and that seed will grow faster and bigger.

00:23:53.600 --> 00:24:08.280
And very interesting. The more you
understand seeds and you think about seeds
during coffee meditation, they will open faster also.

00:24:13.640 --> 00:24:17.720
Do you know the four steps to plant a good karma?

00:24:19.160 --> 00:24:30.160
"Yeah, I do." Oh well, that knowledge is like sunlight on all your good seeds. They are going to grow faster than the other person who doesn't understand them.

00:24:39.080 --> 00:24:41.920
Do you understand the four laws of karma?

00:24:42.640 --> 00:24:49.320
"Yeah, yeah I do."
Well then that's like sunlight on your good seeds,
they're going to grow faster.

00:24:51.840 --> 00:24:53.840
Do you understand the four flowers?

00:24:54.920 --> 00:24:59.320
Or how seeds open?

00:24:59.840 --> 00:25:05.280
And like that. Understand that the more you understand about seeds,

00:25:06.040 --> 00:25:10.880
the more sunlight goes on those seeds
and the faster they grow.

00:25:15.200 --> 00:25:18.600
So keep studying,
keep studying,
keep studying.

00:25:20.120 --> 00:25:29.600
The Knowledge Base has over
five thousand free talks and things to read.

00:25:34.120 --> 00:25:37.120
Do a little bit everyday.
Do ten minutes.

00:25:38.880 --> 00:25:42.080
Then all your good karmas are going to open faster.

00:25:43.880 --> 00:25:50.720
If you don't, then it is like radiation.
It's going to kill your good seeds.

00:25:51.240 --> 00:25:56.560
It won't turn on the bomb. It will turn off the bomb.
The good bomb.

00:25:59.080 --> 00:26:02.520
Ok, next picture,

00:26:02.760 --> 00:26:08.560
this is three sets of the twelve links.

00:26:10.440 --> 00:26:14.960
It's a very simple principle,
I don't have to talk about it much.

00:26:16.040 --> 00:26:20.880
Each time you start this wheel spinning,

00:26:22.320 --> 00:26:26.160
even before the whole wheel spins,

00:26:28.480 --> 00:26:31.640
it will touch another wheel and start another one.

00:26:34.080 --> 00:26:40.880
So this is kind of like all the cogs in the watch
that we showed with Shakespeare.

00:26:47.360 --> 00:26:49.360
Watch my hands...[spinning wheel sounds]

00:26:56.480 --> 00:27:00.120
There's many wheels going on at the same time.

00:27:02.920 --> 00:27:06.160
So don't start them--the bad ones.

00:27:07.880 --> 00:27:11.800
Okay, the next idim we have here, number nine,

00:27:13.280 --> 00:27:16.720
it's a downward staircase.

00:27:20.800 --> 00:27:27.840
Actually this comes from
a short description by Nagarjuna.

00:27:31.040 --> 00:27:37.960
The tendency of the wheel is to spin off another wheel.

00:27:41.040 --> 00:27:54.080
You have one of those three links,
which are negative thoughts, mis-understanding,
then be happy you did a bad thing.

00:27:54.480 --> 00:27:58.160
Then misunderstand seeds in general.

00:27:59.240 --> 00:28:03.080
They trigger two kinds of karma.

00:28:04.000 --> 00:28:08.360
Fresh karma and ripe karma.

00:28:09.080 --> 00:28:13.360
Then those trigger normal human life.

00:28:15.360 --> 00:28:24.720
Seven steps from when your mind
enters your mom up to the time you die

00:28:25.360 --> 00:28:29.680
but, dan chu, unfortunately,

00:28:30.000 --> 00:28:35.160
during those seven, you are doing the first three again.

00:28:37.840 --> 00:28:44.040
Therefore the Wheel of Life tends to spin itself.

00:28:47.000 --> 00:28:50.200
And that's the meaning of the staircase.

00:28:51.680 --> 00:28:58.640
idim number ten is a person in a jail.

00:28:59.760 --> 00:29:04.320
If you succeed in this course,

00:29:07.000 --> 00:29:16.040
I think you should start to feel some panic.
Right now we have the virus going around.
In our town, the first person got it yesterday.

00:29:23.320 --> 00:29:29.440
You can feel the panic and you can--
I don't know, you feel this panic in all the people.

00:29:32.400 --> 00:29:40.800
I think even animals, like the birds and the dog,
they also feel there is something going on.

00:29:43.080 --> 00:29:49.160
And right now only the Buddhist people
in our town have a peaceful mind.

00:29:52.320 --> 00:29:55.320
Why am I talking about that?

00:29:55.840 --> 00:30:00.120
If you really understand the Wheel of Life,

00:30:02.440 --> 00:30:05.520
part of you should be panic.

00:30:08.920 --> 00:30:12.920
You should feel uncomfortable all the time.

00:30:13.600 --> 00:30:17.520
Nothing here is going to go well.

00:30:19.160 --> 00:30:21.560
If I get married,

00:30:22.080 --> 00:30:24.000
if I have kids,

00:30:24.080 --> 00:30:26.040
if I make money,

00:30:26.320 --> 00:30:28.160
if I buy a house,

00:30:28.440 --> 00:30:31.600
if I go to the gym and work out,

00:30:32.360 --> 00:30:36.000
time, in the wheel,
will destroy all of those things.

00:30:39.840 --> 00:30:43.360
I will lose my kids or they will lose me.

00:30:44.600 --> 00:30:49.040
Will lose my husband or wife, or they will lose me.

00:30:49.960 --> 00:30:52.200
Will lose my home.

00:30:53.080 --> 00:30:55.200
Will lose my body.

00:30:55.720 --> 00:31:02.080
Then on one level, you should feel
a little bit panicked to be inside this wheel.

00:31:06.120 --> 00:31:13.320
This picture of a guy in it, this is a modern jail,
okay, it's not these bars anymore.

00:31:16.080 --> 00:31:24.440
I chose the picture for two reasons.
Number one, he's obviously in a jail, he can't get out.

00:31:26.040 --> 00:31:32.200
But number two, it felt to me like he was depressed also.

00:31:33.480 --> 00:31:36.960
I used to teach in the jail.

00:31:38.680 --> 00:31:50.200
We started many years ago. We've been helping prisoners with the ACI courses for about twenty-five years.

00:31:56.160 --> 00:32:00.160
And when you teach them the four steps in the jail,

00:32:01.520 --> 00:32:09.880
you don't have to ask them
what their goal is with the four steps.

00:32:12.080 --> 00:32:18.320
I used to ask them,
"Oh, so you learned the four steps, right?"

00:32:19.040 --> 00:32:22.000
"Yeah."
"What are you using it for?"

00:32:22.440 --> 00:32:29.360
They're not going to say money.
Or girlfriend. Or muscles.

00:32:29.960 --> 00:32:32.520
They just say, "I want to get out."

00:32:33.400 --> 00:32:40.360
And by the way, many prisoners succeeded to get their sentence shorter by using the four steps.

00:32:44.120 --> 00:32:50.880
So this picture--
famous, famous, famous, lam rim saying:

00:32:51.880 --> 00:32:58.080
If you don't realize you're in the jail,
you don't want to get out of the jail.

00:33:02.640 --> 00:33:04.880
Okay, the next picture,

00:33:05.280 --> 00:33:13.280
a strong guy, looks like Stanley,
just kidding, with an axe.

00:33:14.040 --> 00:33:23.000
That represents the three kinds of practices
we're going to use to get out of the wheel.

00:33:29.000 --> 00:33:37.160
In this example, the wheel is like a big tree
that you want to get rid of.

00:33:41.280 --> 00:33:50.840
The sharp axe is your understanding of
emptiness and dependent origination.

00:33:51.040 --> 00:33:55.280
What are those two things in the kitchen?

00:33:56.040 --> 00:34:00.320
"Oh, there is no husband in the kitchen
that doesn't come from me.

00:34:02.000 --> 00:34:06.320
Oh, my husband is yelling at me
because I yelled at my kids."

00:34:07.520 --> 00:34:10.520
That's perfect emptiness and dependent origination.

00:34:12.760 --> 00:34:22.920
I'm not making it simple. I'm making it deep.
That is real emptiness and real dependent origination. Hundred percent.

00:34:26.280 --> 00:34:31.040
So for this big job to get out of this wheel,

00:34:34.040 --> 00:34:36.600
we're going to need three things.

00:34:37.480 --> 00:34:41.160
Number one: a big axe,

00:34:41.680 --> 00:34:46.160
which is you studied the lam rim very well.

00:34:49.080 --> 00:34:56.640
Then, focus--because if you ever cut a tree, you have to hit the same place on the tree every time, otherwise it won't fall down.

00:35:00.640 --> 00:35:02.640
That's shamatha.

00:35:02.800 --> 00:35:04.760
What is shamatha?

00:35:04.760 --> 00:35:06.320
Very deep.

00:35:06.320 --> 00:35:08.160
What is it?

00:35:08.160 --> 00:35:10.080
Meditate every day!

00:35:10.080 --> 00:35:12.200
Shut up and meditate.

00:35:12.200 --> 00:35:15.720
Don't worry about "what is shamatha?"

00:35:16.600 --> 00:35:23.600
Meditate every day.
Start with ten minutes.
Every Sunday, increase by one minute.

00:35:24.120 --> 00:35:26.280
You will get to shamatha.

00:35:27.240 --> 00:35:31.320
Then you need strong arms.

00:35:32.200 --> 00:35:37.040
That's you're treating other people nicely.

00:35:38.120 --> 00:35:41.080
Not hurting other people.

00:35:41.160 --> 00:35:47.400
"So Geshe-la, when should I start?"

00:35:48.960 --> 00:36:00.160
Well if your hair was on fire,
when would you start to put it out?

00:36:01.120 --> 00:36:06.200
So don't ask me, "Geshe-la when should I start?"

00:36:09.120 --> 00:36:17.560
"Can I start tomorrow?"
Yeah, yeah. Your hair caught on fire, you should put it out tomorrow."

00:36:21.000 --> 00:36:24.120
No, act like your hair is on fire.

00:36:27.760 --> 00:36:36.040
No, don't say it that way, it's wrong.
It's wrong to say "act like your hair is on fire."

00:36:38.880 --> 00:36:46.560
"Geshe-la, how do you want me to say it?"
Your hair is on fire. Right now!

00:36:46.920 --> 00:36:49.800
It's not like it's on fire.

00:36:50.600 --> 00:36:52.600
Your hair is on fire.

00:36:53.160 --> 00:36:55.840
So start your practice now.

00:36:56.320 --> 00:36:59.520
By the way, okay, last thing.

00:37:00.320 --> 00:37:06.400
Most of you listening to this,
I know most of you,
you are Buddhist.

00:37:09.120 --> 00:37:15.280
And you have this Buddhist guilt complex.
Guilty--feel guilty.

00:37:18.040 --> 00:37:22.440
"For many years Geshe-la told me to meditate
but I don't meditate everyday.

00:37:25.840 --> 00:37:31.440
And for many years Geshe-la told us to do the six-times book but I don't do it every day.

00:37:34.120 --> 00:37:42.920
And I still yell at my husband or my wife. The emptiness thing doesn't really work in the kitchen."

00:37:45.160 --> 00:37:51.960
So if you're like me, I've known about all this stuff for almost fifty years.

00:37:54.480 --> 00:37:58.960
But then I just get busy and I don't do it.

00:38:00.400 --> 00:38:05.000
Then I feel guilty.
I feel uncomfortable

00:38:05.800 --> 00:38:09.520
People say, "Oh, Geshe-la, you are a Buddhist teacher."

00:38:10.560 --> 00:38:13.160
I'm like, "Yeah, I am a Buddhist teacher."

00:38:13.560 --> 00:38:26.840
But inside I feel guilty.
I didn't do my book. I skipped my meditation today.
I still get upset at Veronica sometimes.

00:38:28.480 --> 00:38:37.200
So what I'm suggesting is just start small.
Start now.

00:38:37.480 --> 00:38:41.240
Do a little meditation.
Start over.

00:38:41.720 --> 00:38:46.600
Pretend it's the first day you heard about Buddhism.

00:38:47.600 --> 00:38:52.600
Just quietly start all your practices again.

00:38:53.720 --> 00:38:58.440
Keep your book. Do your meditation.

00:38:58.520 --> 00:39:03.520
Try to remember "I didn't do anything!" is wrong.

00:39:05.520 --> 00:39:10.160
I'm telling you from my personal experience,

00:39:10.560 --> 00:39:13.840
your Buddhism will go up and down.

00:39:17.080 --> 00:39:19.880
In English we have an expression:

00:39:20.920 --> 00:39:23.880
two steps forward, one step back.

00:39:24.240 --> 00:39:28.000
You practice for two days

00:39:29.120 --> 00:39:31.120
then you fail for one day.

00:39:33.160 --> 00:39:36.760
Don't expect your Buddhism to go like this...

00:39:38.520 --> 00:39:43.280
It's not going to go like that.
I'm telling you it will go like this...

00:39:44.000 --> 00:39:48.280
Good, good, good, good, good, good, mistake.

00:39:48.920 --> 00:39:52.040
Start again.

00:39:52.040 --> 00:39:55.520
Good, good, good, good, good, good, mistake.

00:39:56.080 --> 00:39:59.640
And the whole is going up.

00:40:00.120 --> 00:40:03.120
But it's like this..

00:40:03.440 --> 00:40:06.240
You will have bad days.

00:40:07.800 --> 00:40:11.240
Then just be stubborn.

00:40:12.040 --> 00:40:18.000
You've got to feel guilty if you don't get back to your practice soon.

00:40:20.080 --> 00:40:25.120
For me the guilty is worse than not becoming a Buddha.

00:40:28.280 --> 00:40:31.920
You don't have to feel guilty

00:40:32.480 --> 00:40:36.160
if you just try a little bit tomorrow.

00:40:36.480 --> 00:40:40.160
You don't have to become Buddha in one day.

00:40:40.280 --> 00:40:46.080
Okay, you didn't sit
on your meditation seat for two weeks,

00:40:47.840 --> 00:40:52.680
and your mind is saying
"Oh, I'm a bad person, I'm a bad person..."

00:40:54.160 --> 00:40:56.920
Just tell your mind, "Shut up!"

00:40:57.720 --> 00:41:02.640
Sit down on your meditation seat and start again.

00:41:03.200 --> 00:41:05.200
You're making progress.

00:41:05.760 --> 00:41:07.760
Okay. Good luck!

00:41:07.800 --> 00:41:09.440
See you then.

00:41:09.440 --> 00:41:14.200
Thank you Stanley, and thank you Tim,
and thank you Xiaoping.

00:41:14.720 --> 00:41:19.520
Okay. See you later.

